mt7915: CR6608 MURU record serialisation and in-flight fault attribution

Verified defects in the live MURU record refresh (patches 06/08), found by
reading the station lifecycle against mac80211.c and the mt7996 precedent:

1. mt7915_mac_sta_event (ASSOC/AUTHORIZE/DISASSOC) and the replay in
   mt7915_mac_sta_rc_work both ran without dev->mt76.mutex, so a replay
   snapshotted as CONNECT could land after AUTHORIZE (downgrading the peer
   in firmware, which mac80211 never repeats), or after DISASSOC/removal
   (re-creating a connected record for a torn-down WCID, touching an msta
   mac80211 is about to free).  Both now hold the mutex, exactly as
   mt7996_mac_sta_event / mt7996_mac_sta_rc_work do; sta_add/sta_remove
   already run under it in mac80211.c.

2. __mt7915_mcu_add_sta spent the PERMANENT fault latch and forced a full
   reset when the live mask was lowered between TLV build and send, or
   between send and response, or when the send failed for any reason.
   None of those is firmware evidence: the first two are one-way host
   lowerings (debugfs write, kill switch, a recovery's own disarm) and the
   third includes the -ENOMEM/-ETIMEDOUT a pending recovery produces by
   setting MT76_MCU_RESET.  A stale record is now rebuilt from the live
   mask (bounded), an acknowledged-but-stale record is re-queued for a
   live replay, and a failure inside a pending recovery is attributed to
   that recovery (watchdog -> latch, otherwise disarm + strike).  The same
   gate applies to the STA_REC_UPDATE timeout in mt7915_mcu_parse_response.
   A failure with no recovery pending still latches, as before.

3. After a verified partial reset the records were only replayed when the
   re-arm succeeded, so a refused re-arm (latched, strikes exhausted,
   operator kill during the reset) left firmware records armed while the
   host reported mask 0.  The replay now runs after every verified partial
   reset, converging the records in both directions.

4. A replay that met a reset window was silently dropped (changed bit
   cleared, nothing re-queued) and only band 0's state was consulted.  It
   is now parked back on sta_rc_list with the refresh bit set, checks the
   peer's own phy, and runs again when the band is released
   (mt7915_reconfig_tx_release) or the partial-reset refresh fires.

No new MCU command, no firmware ABI change, no new capability bit.  The
new sta_rec_stale counter in cr6608_ul_muru_state is host telemetry.

